minios-help (1.0.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Keep the native language combo-box appearance while using GTK's list
    popup to avoid blank space for languages near the end of the list
  * Synchronize bundled help with the current MiniOS documentation and derive
    the document set from the sidebar instead of hard-coding section names
  * Use matching rounded frames for the contents and document panes without
    letting their scrollable children overwrite the curved corners
  * Add a VitePress-style, hideable right-side page outline for H2/H3 sections
    with a bold translatable heading, click-to-scroll navigation and accurate
    active-section tracking, including the final section at the bottom
  * Delegate all precompiled-document rendering and styling to minios-gui
  * Require python3-minios-gui 1.3.0 for the updated document renderer
  * Render compact warning and danger notices and hide read-only text carets
  * Add code-block copy feedback and rounded styling for document tables
  * Preserve spaces in Mermaid labels and separate diagrams from nearby text
  * Allow the read-only help viewer to run as root when needed

 -- crims0n <crims0n@minios.dev>  Tue, 01 Sep 2026 02:17:40 +0300

minios-help (1.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Exclude VCS metadata and generated build/test artifacts
  * Add xauth for the Xvfb-based build test suite
  * Synchronize kernel provider, payload, and CondinAPT documentation
  * Regenerate bundled help with the current Markdown compiler

